abstract: >-
  Machine-checked Lean 4 certificates for Gate 0 of Project EXOTIC-CCR:
  Jacobian determinant det DF = -2, three-point collision identities, and
  standard non-injectivity packaging for the announced polynomial map F
  (and det-1 form G), the full algebraic cotangent-lift Theorem B including
  canonical Poisson generator brackets, real-vector-field incompleteness,
  canonical minimal transport core, and a deficiency-to-not-ESS operator
  bridge. Commit ff50f4a2a312591c2e5b26e71eb390ade9164b34 first introduced
  the complete bounded theorem source. The current synchronized artifact
  candidate containing this metadata includes those sources, executable axiom
  auditing, and build provenance. The named theorem
  ExoticCCR.theoremE proves that the canonical minimal X1 transport core is
  not essentially self-adjoint. For that specific canonical minimal operator,
  the chosen Hilbert-basis deficiency indices at +i and -i equal aleph0, and
  all SelfAdjointExtension witnesses are classified bijectively by
  complex-linear isometric equivalences between those eigenspaces; at least
  two distinct witnesses exist, and unitary complex phases inject into
  distinct extension witnesses. The further continuum-sized-family corollary
  uses the external classical cardinality of the complex unit circle and is
  not itself formalized in this Lean artifact. The algebraic
  hamelDeficiencyRank statements remain lower bounds, not an exact Hamel-rank
  result. No arbitrary-operator theorem,
  preferred extension, exact cardinality of the full extension type or
  inequivalence result,
  full historical Theorem F package, strong CCR/Weyl, C-star, CP, channels,
  gates, physical significance, or computational advantage is claimed. The
  historical Theorem E tag v0.1.8-theorem-e targets
  be4f330980f15a503aa582cbadc09c36ecf2ea10, whose reviewed theorem source
  anchor is a6bb091c05943cfcf35c405659e57df93ab8bb3d.
  No release version, release tag, version DOI, or Zenodo DOI exists for the
  proposed Theorem F freeze. The lakefile version 0.1.8-dev is development
  metadata only, not a release or Zenodo version.
